tar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-24T13:28:39Z","updated_at":"2026-05-24T13:38:05Z","body":"Can confirm with current master and current macos, wrong base color is set in both light and dark themes.\n\nI think the intent here was to try to use the actual OS theme color as godot base color:\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/fa6cad230f638d65a5a897008c5fc512edc237ad/editor/themes/editor_theme_manager.cpp#L377-L380\n\nI don't think it makes sense and I'm pretty sure that's not what most users expect to happen because in all other apps \"Follow System Theme\" just picks between light/dark presets. It looks especially broken in light macos theme because it happens to pick pure white which doesnt work with the light theme. I dont have a windows machine to test atm but I assume if it doesn't look broken on windows (or other OSes) it happens by pure chance because the OS system color happens to fit better.\n\nThis block above already switches between Default/Light presets based on luminance:\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/fa6cad230f638d65a5a897008c5fc512edc237ad/editor/themes/editor_theme_manager.cpp#L304-L312\n\nP.S In my testing I got not exactly the same wrong colors as in the author's video, but different wrong colors, which is also a sign that the behavior can get more unpredictable and confusing depending on OS version.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4528865145/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]